# Tetris-lite (falling single blocks, rows clear), in Intent v0.6.0.
# GENERATED by gen_tetris.py - edit that file, not this one.
#   ./intent build gemini-build/build-11-tetris-lite/tetris.intent -o build/tetris && build/tetris
# Left/right move the block, down drops it faster. A full row disappears.

The board is 8 wide and 14 high.

The px starts at 4.
The py starts at 1.
The landed starts at 0.
The clear starts at 0.
The clock starts at 0.
The score starts at 0.
The lines start at 0.
The delay starts at 8.

The alpha starts at 0.
The bravo starts at 0.
The charlie starts at 0.
The delta starts at 0.
The echo starts at 0.
The foxtrot starts at 0.
The golf starts at 0.
The hotel starts at 0.
The india starts at 0.
The juliet starts at 0.
The kilo starts at 0.
The lima starts at 0.
The mike starts at 0.
The november starts at 0.

Cells is a collection where each cell has an x (number) and a y (number).

# --- gravity gets faster as rows are cleared (timers are fixed, so a fast clock counts up to a delay)
The delay is always 2 if the lines are at least 18, otherwise 8 minus the lines divided by 3.
Every 50 milliseconds, the clock increases by 1.

# --- moving
# Bug found: "if the px is over 1 and no cell has ..." is refused ("I don't know the word no");
# "any"/"no" only work as the FIRST condition, so the order of the two conditions is forced.
When the left key is pressed, if no cell has an x equal to the px minus 1 and a y equal to the py, the px decreases by 1 if the px is over 1.
When the right key is pressed, if no cell has an x equal to the px plus 1 and a y equal to the py, the px increases by 1 if the px is under 8.
When the down key is pressed, the clock becomes the delay.

# --- one step of gravity, in order
Every 50 milliseconds, if the clock is at least the delay and the py is 14, the landed becomes 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if any cell has an x equal to the px and a y equal to the py plus 1, the landed becomes 1 if the clock is at least the delay.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the clock is at least the delay and the landed is 0, the py increases by 1.

Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 1, the alpha increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 2, the bravo increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 3, the charlie increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 4, the delta increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 5, the echo increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 6, the foxtrot increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 7, the golf increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 8, the hotel increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 9, the india increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 10, the juliet increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 11, the kilo increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 12, the lima increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 13, the mike increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1 and the py is 14, the november increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1, add a cell whose x is the px and whose y is the py.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1, the px becomes a random number between 1 and 8.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1, the py becomes 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1, the score increases by 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the landed is 1, the landed becomes 0.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the clock is at least the delay, the clock becomes 0.

